Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:19:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Data loader: numpy BOS index, and
 ScheduledBatches.close()

The timed run's first shard builds its partial BOS index on the main thread before step 0, with
the GPU idle. np.flatnonzero gives the same ascending int64 indices as torch's nonzero (the
loader's torch ops run single-threaded under torchrun): partial index 12.8 -> 1.7 ms, the
background full scan 265 -> 69 ms per shard (CPU measurements). The faster scan also widens
the margin before a shard's partial index could run out ahead of its full scan.

ScheduledBatches.close() closes the loader, releasing the shards it holds; the final
validation uses it (next commit).

tools/tests/test_token_stream_identical.py replays the record's whole 1194-step schedule and the
validation through upstream 4ea6b93's data.py and this one: every batch byte-identical (rule 1).

